[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318020105","pull_request_review_id":4381250069,"id":3318020105,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7FxPgJ","diff_hunk":"@@ -265,7 +267,7 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeAnimation::_process(ProcessState &p_pro\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tAnimationMixer::PlaybackInfo pi = p_playback_info;\n-\t\tpi.start = 0.0;\n+\t\tpi.start = playback_start;\n \t\tpi.end = playback_end;","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_tree.cpp","commit_id":"38a63bdab1a63fdd34541d36c43c090311119f52","original_commit_id":"38a63bdab1a63fdd34541d36c43c090311119f52","user":{"login":"chocola-mint","id":56677134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Njc3MTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56677134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint","html_url":"https://github.com/chocola-mint","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"```suggestion\n\t\tpi.end = anim_size;\n```\n@TokageItLab \n(Sorry for the late reply)\n\nI actually came up with a different solution.\n\nThe root issue is that `AnimationBlendTree` was created before animation sections were implemented, and so had its own logic for processing and looping its own timeline section. To keep this looping logic working as-is, the right thing to do would be to have `AnimationMixer` pretend that the animation is being played with no sections. (Thus using 0 for `pi.start` and `anim_size` for `pi.end`)\n\nAlternatively uniting the timeline section processing with the one in `AnimationMixer` can also be more desirable, but I suspect this would be tricky to implement. I'll leave the decision up to you.\n\n(Note: The fix I have here works for https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119769 and does not break https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118101 either)","created_at":"2026-05-28T13:16:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T13:17:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318020105","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318020105"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318020105"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318020105/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":271,"original_line":271,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":48,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318227865","pull_request_review_id":4381517154,"id":3318227865,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7FyCOZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -265,7 +267,7 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeAnimation::_process(ProcessState &p_pro\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tAnimationMixer::PlaybackInfo pi = p_playback_info;\n-\t\tpi.start = 0.0;\n+\t\tpi.start = playback_start;\n \t\tpi.end = playback_end;","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_tree.cpp","commit_id":"38a63bdab1a63fdd34541d36c43c090311119f52","original_commit_id":"38a63bdab1a63fdd34541d36c43c090311119f52","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Considering that `pi.start` was always 0, I think this is a reasonable fix. Therefore, we will deprecate `playback_end`.","created_at":"2026-05-28T13:49:26Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T13:49:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318227865","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318227865"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318227865"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318227865/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":271,"original_line":271,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3318020105,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":48,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318262438","pull_request_review_id":4381558809,"id":3318262438,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7FyKqm","diff_hunk":"@@ -265,7 +267,7 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeAnimation::_process(ProcessState &p_pro\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tAnimationMixer::PlaybackInfo pi = p_playback_info;\n-\t\tpi.start = 0.0;\n+\t\tpi.start = playback_start;\n \t\tpi.end = playback_end;","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_tree.cpp","commit_id":"38a63bdab1a63fdd34541d36c43c090311119f52","original_commit_id":"38a63bdab1a63fdd34541d36c43c090311119f52","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I tested the removal of `playback_end`, but it still doesn't work correctly. If I do that, when looping for a duration shorter than the animation length in `custom_timeline`, it ends up calling a method that's out of bounds; In other words, this does not re-cause the AnimationPlayer bug, but re-cause the bug in the AnimationTree (so https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116002 was also caused in AnimationTree).\r\n\r\nMRP (loop between 0-0.5 and method placed 1s):\r\n[b-tree-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28349626/b-tree-bug.zip)\r\n\r\nTherefore, introducing `playback_start` would be the better approach.","created_at":"2026-05-28T13:54:20Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T14:02:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318262438","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318262438"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318262438"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318262438/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":271,"original_line":271,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3318020105,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":48,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318445898","pull_request_review_id":4381786505,"id":3318445898,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fy3dK","diff_hunk":"","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_tree.cpp","commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","original_commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","user":{"login":"chocola-mint","id":56677134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Njc3MTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56677134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint","html_url":"https://github.com/chocola-mint","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"(GitHub broke my comment. This is supposed to be referring to R208 and R209, the two lines with `fposmod`)\n\nThis looks off to me. The modulo operation here can cause `cur_playback_time` to be moved before `start_offset` if custom timeline is active. And it'd also mean that the loop detection code below would likely not function properly as well.\n\nHowever, I did test the code and it's working for both https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119769 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118101, so I don't have a strong case against it either.\n\nI do recommend more testing though.","created_at":"2026-05-28T14:21:37Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T14:26:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318445898","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318445898"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318445898"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318445898/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":206,"original_start_line":206,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":207,"original_line":207,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318494406","pull_request_review_id":4381848657,"id":3318494406,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7FzDTG","diff_hunk":"","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_tree.cpp","commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","original_commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Since these extend both ends of anim_size, this code shouldn’t be incorrect. It’s true that it’s a bit odd because looped_flag isn’t linked to custom_timeline, but that’s a separate issue that needs to be addressed independently of the reported bug. We might need to provide a looped signal specifically for custom_timeline.","created_at":"2026-05-28T14:28:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T14:28:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318494406","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318494406"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318494406"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318494406/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":206,"original_start_line":206,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":207,"original_line":207,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3318445898,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318578743","pull_request_review_id":4381954559,"id":3318578743,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7FzX43","diff_hunk":"","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_tree.cpp","commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","original_commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","user":{"login":"chocola-mint","id":56677134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Njc3MTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56677134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint","html_url":"https://github.com/chocola-mint","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`cur_time` is taken from `p_playback_info.time`, and `cur_playback_time = cur_time + playback_start`, so the range of `cur_playback_time` would be `[playback_start, playback_start + playback_end]`. Therefore taking modulo of `anim_size` would result in values before `playback_start` once `cur_time` is in the range of `[anim_size, max(anim_size, playback_start + playback_end)]`.\n\nI suspect that a looping custom timeline with non-zero `start_offset` would behave incorrectly because of this, but it's also possible that `AnimationMixer` is clamping the playback time back within `playback_start` and `playback_end` automatically, so it looks like it's working. (Though in this case I think a bit of the delta time would get lost to the clamping every time it loops)","created_at":"2026-05-28T14:40:21Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T14:43:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318578743","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318578743"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318578743"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318578743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":206,"original_start_line":206,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":207,"original_line":207,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3318445898,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318652674","pull_request_review_id":4382045578,"id":3318652674,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fzp8C","diff_hunk":"","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_tree.cpp","commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","original_commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","user":{"login":"chocola-mint","id":56677134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Njc3MTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56677134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint","html_url":"https://github.com/chocola-mint","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Again, I don't actually have a strong case against this. It's a tricky situation that we have to do additional processing for custom timeline sections on top of `AnimationMixer`'s section processing, and it's surprising to me that this is working properly at all. I feel like I'm missing some edge cases, and I do hope that I'm wrong about this.\n\nI do think this code should be revisited to address how `looped_flag` functions here later, but the current solution is fine for addressing a release blocker.","created_at":"2026-05-28T14:51:40Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T14:51:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318652674","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318652674"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318652674"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318652674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":206,"original_start_line":206,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":207,"original_line":207,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3318445898,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318763122","pull_request_review_id":4382187098,"id":3318763122,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7F0E5y","diff_hunk":"","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_tree.cpp","commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","original_commit_id":"fd332fb24946a20629e625cb648f7eb03b339191","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I see. I confirmed that it breaks when using “Backward.” The following MRPs use the same key for both ‘Discrete’ and “Continuous+nearest”; Since Discrete and Method should return the same result.\r\n\r\n[b-tree-bug2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28352258/b-tree-bug2.zip)\r\n\r\nWhen “custom_timeline” is disabled, a one-frame delay in “Backward” is the intended behavior (as I mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/11139#discussioncomment-11231933), but in MRP, it's clear that the retrieval range is incorrect.\r\n\r\n@chocola-mint I'm a bit busy right now, so if you could take over this PR and create a PR to fix it, I'll be able to review it.\r\n","created_at":"2026-05-28T15:07:56Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T15:29:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318763122","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318763122"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119846#discussion_r3318763122"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119846"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3318763122/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":206,"original_start_line":206,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":207,"original_line":207,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3318445898,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}]